# std/ls — one of the file tools (std/files holds the source they share).
# The help is a HERE-STRING so it lives in this expression, which is stripped
# from the tree the build sees: editing the docs re-keys this tool's ArgTree and
# nothing it builds from.
HELP=<<END
List a directory: one entry per line, directories (and source trees) with a trailing `/`. Paths start at the root of the tree this tool runs over (the conversation, unless `in` names another) and traverse code references, for example feature/dirty/src. Prefer this over `ls` via bash. Listings are cut at 1000 entries.
@param [path] Directory to list; omit for the root itself.
@in
END
IMAGE=run --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/rustc --src:@=DEEP-DEPS/files
curry --base=$IMAGE --op=ls --help=$HELP
